    <h2>The coffee</h2>
    <p>
        Our espresso is a seasonal blend from a small roaster two valleys over, chosen to taste good with butter and sugar rather than on its
        own in a cupping bowl: chocolate, a little stone fruit, not too sharp. Sam dials it in every morning before the doors open.
    </p>
    <p>
        The filter changes every Tuesday. It is brewed by the batch and never sits more than half an hour; after that it goes in the iced coffee.
    </p>

    <h2>The kettle</h2>
    <p>
        The café is named for it. The chai is simmered on the stove each morning from whole spices: cardamom, cinnamon bark, ginger, clove and
        black pepper, with strong black tea and milk. It is not sweet unless you ask. There is loose-leaf tea in pots, and mint from the yard in
        summer.
    </p>

    <h2>Sitting in</h2>
    <p>
        There are eleven tables, a long bench in the window and two on the sidewalk in good weather. Read more about finding us, parking and
        the quiet hours on the <a href="/visit/">visit page</a>.
    </p>
